  "_notes": "Native-shopper glossary for product TITLES (and option labels/meta built from them) on dresslikemommy.com, 20 locales. HOW TO APPLY: (1) Translate the English title around these terms; when an English title contains a key (case-insensitive, also 'Mommy and Me', 'Mommy & Me', 'Mom & Me'), use the locale value, never a word-for-word rendering. (2) 'Mommy & Me' / 'Daddy & Me' values are gender-NEUTRAL for the child (mother/father + child): use them for every Mommy & Me product, including mother-son items. Use the Mother Daughter / Mother Son / Father Son / Father Daughter values ONLY when the English title says Daughter/Girl or Son/Boy. (3) Prefer the natural 'for' construction (de 'für Mama und Kind', da 'til mor og barn', no 'til mamma og barn', nl 'voor mama en kind', el 'για μαμά και παιδί', he 'לאמא ולילד', ko '엄마와 아이 커플룩', ja '親子ペアルック' as head noun with ママと子ども, es 'para mamá y peque'); never the pronoun forms (Mamá y yo, Mama en ik, Mor og mig, Μαμά και Εγώ, אמא ואני, 엄마와 나, ママと私, Мама и я, Mamãe e eu, Maman et moi, Mamma e Me, Mamma och jag, Mama i ja, Äiti ja minä, माँ और मैं). (4) Christmas / Boże Narodzenie style values show noun / adjective-or-compound-prefix; choose the form the grammar needs (de Weihnachts- compounds, nl kerst-, da/no jule-, sv jul-, fi joulu-). ALTERNATIVES / HARD CALLS: es neutral child = 'peque' (Spain-coloured but understood in LatAm; fallbacks 'mamá y mini', 'mamá y niños'; 'mamá y yo' is searched in US-Hispanic queries but is the calque the editors rejected, keep out of titles). pt-BR neutral = 'mamãe e filhos' (alternatives 'mamãe e mini', 'mãe e filho(a)'). it 'mamma e bambino' (alt 'mamma e bimbo/bimbi'). he child = 'ילד' generic-masculine, use 'ילד/ה' only in size labels. ar child 'طفل' with possessive 'طفلها/طفله'. hi 'बच्चे' generic. ja: 親子ペアルック / 親子コーデ is the head shopping term (covers mother AND father); keep お揃い (not おそろい) consistent; 母息子 not 母子 (母子 reads as mother-and-baby health). ko: 커플룩 (site term) or 패밀리룩 for family; 엄마와 딸 may also be 모녀룩; father-son alt 부자룩; NEVER 맞춤 (tailored) for matching, never mix 시밀러룩 into one page. ru: 'рождественский' for Christmas; 'новогодний' is a different holiday and only for English New Year. Family = 'фэмили лук' (alt 'одинаковая одежда для всей семьи'). pl 'family look' is genuine Polish retail usage (alt 'stroje rodzinne', 'pasujące stroje dla rodziny'). da/no/nl/sv/fi 'strik/strikk/breisel/stickat/neule' are KNIT words; never jersey/tricot (nl tricot, da/no jersey) for chunky knit; ro tricot and ru трикотаж are correct knitwear words in their own language. Cardigan products: use 'Cardigans' value, not 'Sweaters' (nl vesten, fr gilets, sv koftor, de Strickjacken). Sweatshirts vs Hoodies: keep distinct (nl uses 'sweaters' for sweatshirt, so add 'sweatshirt' wording if it clashes with 'truien'). Sources: PRODUCT_TRANSLATION_QA.md and TRANSLATION_QA.md sweeps; supersedes the 'Mommy & Me' / 'Daddy & Me' / 'Mother Daughter' entries in ops/content/translation_glossary.json for product titles. Native-editor review by model, not a paid human review.",
